/* All interactions are local demonstrations. This preview never calls Ascend APIs. */
'use strict';
const pages = [
 ['overview','Review overview','The review','/','The clearest opportunity is to reduce decisions before the work starts. Several pages also confuse unfinished product features with missing student progress.','Preserve the current concept and gradient. Make the next action specific, keep examples separate, and show detail only when it helps a decision.'],
 ['welcome','Welcome','Entry & direction','/welcome','The furniture-led scene does not clearly explain how Ascend helps people prepare for work or why an employer should trust readiness evidence.','Review three purposeful motion concepts and a one-minute explainer draft. Lead with student support and explainable evidence for employers. Keep planned capabilities and intended benefits clearly labelled.'],
 ['auth','Sign in & account','Entry & direction','/login','Login redirects to a welcome modal. A student coming from a tool needs to know they will return to that task; the Google chooser must remain available.','Show the destination above the sign-in action. Use one clear Google action, with email as an alternative. Keep account switching explicit.'],
 ['home','Student home','Entry & direction','/','The selected role is shown, yet the incomplete-profile hero still says “find a direction.” Several long workspace descriptions compete with the next action.','Use the saved role consistently. Make the next task concrete, name why it matters, and make saved work directly accessible.'],
 ['profile','Your profile','Entry & direction','/profile','The profile asks for many sections at once and implies that phone and favourite subjects block exploration. The saved narrative and chosen track can also disagree.','Show one editable section at a time, explain optional information, and review imported facts before saving. Use the same record across all tools.'],
 ['discovery','Discovery & comparison','Entry & direction','/discover','Compare, card opening and role selection compete inside the same role card. Tour setup adds a decision before someone sees the work.','Keep role discovery and comparison. Separate Learn / Compare / Choose. Start the selected workplace directly, with other stops available afterwards.'],
 ['tour','Workplace tour','Entry & direction','/discover','The user has to plan a tour before experiencing it. A workplace needs distinct, meaningful stops rather than another set of role descriptions.','Keep the workplace-based 3D direction. Connect the customer desk, team handover and decision point to what the person would actually do.'],
 ['practice','Practice hub','Practise & improve','/practice','One live assessment shares the page with two unreleased tools and an autoplay explanation. Returning students must browse the product again.','Lead with the available assessment and existing feedback. Keep explanation optional and label planned modules without presenting them as the next task.'],
 ['assessment','Role assessment','Practise & improve','/practice/readiness','The entry offers a retake count before useful feedback. Published older content may still be text-based; new interaction support alone does not convert authored questions.','One scenario, four kinds of response, one 15-minute deadline. Keep instructions short, show save state and provide an untimed format rehearsal before the real start.'],
 ['result','Assessment feedback','Practise & improve','/practice/readiness/results','The readout is long, mixes measured scores with illustrative benchmark lines, and promotes unreleased simulations. “Days you worked” counts situations.','Lead with what the evidence showed and one improvement. Expand the supporting work. Remove invented comparison benchmarks and direct students to an available activity.'],
 ['history','Past assessments','Practise & improve','/practice/readiness/results','The list mixes jobs, repeats “Open,” and leads with scores without helping explain different task coverage.','Filter by role, show which situations were completed, label result links clearly, and avoid implying progress when attempts are not comparable.'],
 ['interviews','Interview preparation','Practise & improve','/interview','Another feature hub repeats a long walkthrough before the student can practise. Its time estimate differs from the actual ten-minute interview setup.','Offer two distinct actions: one question or the full ten-minute interview. Keep saved sessions one click away and the unreleased story bank secondary.'],
 ['interview','Interview room','Practise & improve','/interview/practice','Voice versus typing is offered after Join. Repeated focus areas, round, interviewer and optional coaching create a crowded setup.','Choose how to answer first. Show role and one focus, put optional settings behind disclosure, then start one ten-minute session.'],
 ['questions','Question practice','Practise & improve','/interview/questions','“Answered badly” and “WENT BADLY” make a practice space feel judgemental. Filters dominate. The source’s “Next question” currently closes the answer dialog.','Lead with a specific improvement and one question. Search stays available; feedback names what to change and Next actually opens another question.'],
 ['stories','Story bank','Practise & improve','/stories','This is globally disabled today, but the wording suggests doing more work will unlock it. Those are different conditions.','State that the feature is not released. Link to the available question practice. A future story builder should use Situation / Action / Result with factual review.'],
 ['missions','Role missions','Practise & improve','/practice/missions','The route is not built. Long readiness-versus-proficiency wording makes the missing capability harder to understand.','Be direct about availability and offer a useful existing activity. Keep future mission concepts visibly separate from usable tools.'],
 ['presence','Professional Presence','Prepare to apply','/resume','Saved work is absent from the hub while full sample documents and automated walkthroughs occupy the main view.','Lead with the document the student is working on. Keep Resume, LinkedIn and Job Fit as direct destinations with a short explanation of each.'],
 ['resume','Resume Builder','Prepare to apply','/resume/build','In the signed-in entry, the account’s name appears above sample work and education. Existing documents sit in a small selector while a new build dominates.','Return to saved resumes first. Use only the student’s facts in their document; label a fully anonymous example separately. Keep edit, review and download together.'],
 ['linkedin','LinkedIn Profile Builder','Prepare to apply','/profile/professional','Copy actions are by the section, while Keep actions are far below. Generic rewrite prompts can mention work the student has never done.','Give each section its own editor, optional improvement, save state and copy action. Explain that copying does not update LinkedIn automatically.'],
 ['jobfit','Job Fit Analyzer','Prepare to apply','/job-fit','The blank entry shows prior scoring counts and negative question-history wording before a posting is supplied. It distracts from the current decision.','Paste the description first. Then show requirement → evidence → next action. Keep underlying history on demand; distinguish “not demonstrated” from “cannot do.”'],
 ['journey','Your journey','Progress & account','/journey','The journey catalogue labels some stages unavailable even when another entry point can open the tool. Progress and product release status are mixed.','Separate student progress from product availability. Keep completed work, next available work and planned modules visually distinct.'],
 ['passport','Career Passport','Progress & account','/passport','The page is globally closed, but its explanation suggests enough student evidence would open it.','Tell the student the Passport is not released, and link to their real assessment results now. Preview the evidence record separately without issuing or sharing anything.'],
 ['opportunities','Opportunities','Progress & account','/opportunities','A primary navigation item ends at “This part isn’t built yet,” with no useful action beyond Back.','Make availability visible before entering. Offer the existing Job Fit tool for a posting the student has already found; do not show imaginary jobs.'],
 ['settings','Settings','Progress & account','/settings','Settings offers profile editing and deletion but no appearance controls. Theme is in the avatar menu instead.','Put account and appearance together. Keep data deletion separate and preserve a deliberate confirmation.'],
 ['college','College home','Other audiences','/for/colleges','All five features are planned. The access form sits after them, and “Send request” only opens an email draft.','Lead with the placement-team need and an honest pilot access handoff. Show a labelled workflow illustration, not invented cohort analytics.'],
 ['employer','Employer home','Other audiences','/for/employers','All features are planned, and the generic access form uses a college-specific example for “Your role.”','Lead with evaluating capability for a particular role. Use employer language and an explicit email handoff, with draft-copy fallback.'],
 ['admin','Admin authoring','Administration','/admin','Roles, mappings, questions and media are split across document tabs. Student preview and publication readiness are not one coherent workspace.','Anchor authoring to a role. Edit the scenario, choose a response format, check the skill mapping, preview as a student and review the draft before publishing.']
].map(([id,title,group,path,friction,proposal])=>({id,title,group,path,friction,proposal}));
const $=s=>document.querySelector(s);
const esc=s=>String(s??'').replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
const state={page:'overview',notes:true,mobile:false,profileTab:'Basics',tourStop:0,tourOn:false,compare:[],assessmentStarted:false,assessmentMoment:0,assessmentAnswers:{},assessmentReview:false,interviewMode:'Type',interviewStarted:false,interviewQuestion:0,interviewAnswers:[],question:0,questionFeedback:false,resumeTab:'Edit',resumeLayout:'Classic',resumeName:'A. Sample',linkedinSaved:{},jobResult:false,adminTab:'Scenario',adminRole:'Customer Success Associate',adminFormat:'Decision cards',adminSaved:false,historyRole:'All roles',cohortDraft:false,profileSaved:false};
const roles=[['Customer Success Associate','CUSTOMER','Help customers get a clear answer and a reliable next step.','Customer desk'],['Operations Coordinator','LOGISTICS','Keep priorities, deliveries and teams moving together.','Operations floor'],['Operations Executive','RETAIL','Help a shop floor run smoothly through the day.','Shop floor']];
const questions=['Tell me about something you had to learn quickly with nobody to teach you.','Describe a time you had more to do than time to do it in.','How would you tell a customer something they will not want to hear?'];
const button=(label,action,style='primary',attrs='')=>`<button type="button" class="${style}" data-action="${action}" ${attrs}>${label}</button>`;
const link=(label,id,style='textlink')=>`<a class="${style}" href="#${id}">${label}</a>`;
const badge=(label,kind='')=>`<span class="badge ${kind}">${label}</span>`;
const panel=(title,copy,extra='',cls='')=>`<section class="panel ${cls}"><h3>${title}</h3><p>${copy}</p>${extra}</section>`;
const rolepill=()=>'<div class="rolepill"><small>Your chosen role</small>Customer Success Associate</div>';
const title=(head,copy,role=false)=>`<div class="screenhead"><div><h2>${head}</h2><p>${copy}</p></div>${role?rolepill():''}</div>`;
const section=(head,right='')=>`<div class="sectiontitle"><h3>${head}</h3>${right}</div>`;
const fileart=()=>'<div class="fileart" aria-hidden="true">YOUR NEXT CHAPTER<b>Make your<br>work visible.</b><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>';
const hero=(eyebrow,head,copy,cta,art=fileart())=>`<section class="hero"><div><span class="eyebrow">${eyebrow}</span><h2>${head}</h2><p>${copy}</p>${cta}</div><div>${art}</div></section>`;
const shell=(body,active='Home')=>`<header class="appbar"><a class="appbrand" href="#welcome"><svg width="25" height="28" viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 41L24 8L42 41M16 41L24 26L32 41" stroke="#9682ef" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>ASCEND</a><nav class="appnav" aria-label="Concept navigation">${[['Home','home'],['Discover','discovery'],['Practice','practice'],['Opportunities','opportunities']].map(([t,id])=>`<a href="#${id}" class="${active===t?'active':''}">${t}</a>`).join('')}</nav><a class="avatar" href="#settings" aria-label="Open sample account settings">A</a></header><div class="screen">${body}</div>`;
function overview(){return `<div class="screen"><div class="overviewlead"><span class="eyebrow">Ascend, from a student's point of view</span><h2>Less figuring it out.<br><em>More moving forward.</em></h2><p>The product has useful tools. The next improvement is making the path between them feel obvious, consistent and worth the student's time.</p></div><div class="grid3">${[['home','Clear next actions','Say what to do for the chosen role, using what is already known.'],['resume','Trust the record','Keep sample content, saved work and AI suggestions visibly separate.'],['result','Useful feedback','Turn a score into one concrete improvement and an available next step.']].map(([id,h,p])=>`<a href="#${id}" class="auditcard">${badge('Start here','guide')}<h3>${h} ↗</h3><p>${p}</p></a>`).join('')}</div>${section('Explore the proposed screens',badge('Desktop + mobile · light + dark'))}<div class="overviewlist">${pages.slice(1).map(p=>`<div class="row"><div><strong>${p.title}</strong><small>${p.group}</small></div>${link('Preview →',p.id)}</div>`).join('')}</div>${section('What was checked')}<div class="panel"><p>All 27 public entry URLs were visited in a fresh browser. Returning-student pages and one existing assessment result were inspected in the signed-in browser. Source review covers form behaviour, availability gates and admin authoring.</p><p>Public interaction checks cover navigation, theme, setup, comparison and account gates. Signed-in saving, paid AI generation, live recording, email sending, deletion and publishing remain untested. The preview is a design recommendation, not a certification that every feature works.</p></div></div>`}
function home(){return shell(`${title('Welcome back.','Your next step is about the role you chose.',true)}${hero('Your next move','Practise explaining<br><em>what you can do.</em>','Use one concrete example in a Customer Success Associate interview. Start with a single question, or return to your saved work.',link('Practise one answer →','questions','primary'),'<div class="message" style="background:#073c3433;border-color:#ffffff30;color:#e9f6ef"><strong style="color:#b9e4d0">WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong>Answer a question.<br>Review one improvement.<br>Try again in your own words.</div>')}<div class="split"><div>${section('Your workspace')}<div class="grid3">${panel('Explore the role','See the work before committing.',link('Open Discovery →','discovery'))}${panel('Try a work shift','One role. Fifteen minutes.',link('Open assessment →','assessment'))}${panel('Prepare to apply','Resume, LinkedIn and job fit.',link('Open your tools →','presence'))}</div>${section('Pick up your work',badge('Illustrative saved-work state'))}<div class="panel"><div class="row"><div><strong>Resume · Customer Success Associate</strong><small>Your latest version, ready to review.</small></div>${link('Continue','resume','secondary')}</div><div class="row"><div><strong>LinkedIn profile</strong><small>Review the headline and About section.</small></div>${link('Continue','linkedin','secondary')}</div></div></div><aside>${section('Your direction')}<div class="panel"><ol class="journeyline"><li class="done"><strong>Role chosen</strong><p>Customer Success Associate</p></li><li class="now"><strong>Build your evidence</strong><p>Practise the work and your interview answers.</p></li><li><strong>Prepare your application</strong><p>Bring your experience into your resume.</p></li></ol>${link('View your journey →','journey')}</div><p class="note">Need to add contact details? ${link('Edit profile','profile')}</p></aside></div>`)}
function profile(){const tabs=['Basics','Education','Experience','Interests'];let form='';if(state.profileTab==='Basics')form=`<div class="fieldgrid"><label>Name<input value="Sample student" autocomplete="off"></label><label>City<input placeholder="e.g. Chennai"></label><label class="wide">Where are you now?<select><option>Studying or recently graduated</option><option>Working or looking for my next role</option></select></label><label>Phone <small>Optional until you need it on your resume</small><input type="tel" placeholder="Add when you’re ready"></label><label>LinkedIn or portfolio <small>Optional</small><input type="url" placeholder="https://"></label></div>`;else if(state.profileTab==='Education')form=`<div class="fieldgrid"><label>Course<input placeholder="e.g. B.Com"></label><label>College<input placeholder="Where you study"></label><label>Graduation year<input inputmode="numeric" placeholder="e.g. 2027"></label><label>Subjects you enjoy <small>Optional</small><input placeholder="e.g. Marketing"></label></div>`;else if(state.profileTab==='Experience')form=`<label>A project, internship or job<textarea placeholder="What did you work on? What was your part?"></textarea></label><label>Tools or skills you used<input placeholder="e.g. Google Sheets, customer communication"></label>`;else form=`<p class="smallcopy">Choose the work you are curious about. You can still explore other roles.</p><div class="chips">${['Customer support','Operations','Retail','Banking','Technology'].map(t=>button(t,'interest','',`aria-pressed="false"`)).join('')}</div><label>What matters in your next role? <small>Optional</small><textarea placeholder="Location, working hours, interests or a direction you want to explore."></textarea></label>`;return shell(`${title('Your profile','A few useful details. Build the rest as you go.')}<div class="split"><div class="panel"><div class="sectionnav">${tabs.map(t=>button(t,'profile-tab','',`data-value="${t}" aria-pressed="${t===state.profileTab}"`)).join('')}</div>${form}<div class="actions">${button('Save this section','profile-save')}<span class="smallcopy" id="profile-status">${state.profileSaved?'Saved in this preview':'Preview changes stay on this page'}</span></div></div><aside class="stack">${panel('You can explore now','A phone number or favourite subject is not a reason to delay exploring a role.',link('Continue to Discovery →','discovery'))}${panel('Already have a resume?','Import it, then review the facts before keeping them.',button('See import review','profile-import','secondary'))}</aside></div>`)}
function discovery(){return shell(`${title('Find work you can picture yourself doing.','Learn about a role, compare your options, then choose your direction.')} ${hero('Your chosen role','Step inside<br><em>customer success.</em>','See how a customer question moves from a first reply to a team handover.',link('Enter the workplace →','tour','primary'),'<div class="tourblank" style="height:190px"><div class="desk"></div></div>')}${section('Explore roles',button('Choose industries','industries','secondary'))}<div class="grid3">${roles.map(([name,kind,copy,place],i)=>`<article class="panel rolecard"><div class="symbol" aria-hidden="true">${['◈','⇄','▥'][i]}</div><span class="eyebrow">${kind}</span><h3>${name}</h3><p>${copy}</p>${i===0?badge('Your chosen role','earned'):badge(place)}<div class="actions">${button('Explore role →','role-detail','textlink',`data-value="${i}"`)}<label><input type="checkbox" data-compare="${i}" ${state.compare.includes(i)?'checked':''}>Compare</label></div></article>`).join('')}</div><div id="comparebar" class="comparebar" ${state.compare.length?'':'hidden'}><span id="compare-count">${state.compare.length} roles selected</span>${button('Compare roles →','compare','primary',state.compare.length<2?'disabled':'')}</div>`,'Discover')}
const stops=[['Customer desk','Listen before you promise.','A customer’s delivery is late. Find out what is confirmed before sending an update.'],['Team handover','Make the next step easy to pick up.','Leave the issue, current status, owner and promised update time for your colleague.'],['Decision point','Choose what you can stand behind.','Separate what you know from what you still need to check. Escalate decisions outside your authority.']];
function tour(){const [h,head,copy]=stops[state.tourStop];return shell(`${title('Step inside customer success.','A short workplace tour. Look around, then try a decision.')}<div class="split"><div><div class="tourframe">${state.tourOn?'<iframe title="Illustrative customer success workplace tour" src="/previews/ascend-role-tour-3d.html" sandbox="allow-scripts"></iframe>':'<div class="tourblank"><div class="desk"></div></div>'}<div class="tourcaption">${h} · ${head}</div></div><div class="actions">${button(state.tourOn?'Stop 3D tour':'Play 3D workplace tour','tour-play','secondary')}<small>Illustrative workplace · motion is optional</small></div></div><div class="panel"><div class="sectionnav">${stops.map((s,i)=>button(s[0],'tour-stop','',`data-value="${i}" aria-pressed="${i===state.tourStop}"`)).join('')}</div><span class="eyebrow">${h}</span><h2>${head}</h2><p>${copy}</p><div class="notice">The role is about making a reliable next step clear to the customer and the team.</div><div class="actions">${state.tourStop<2?button('Next stop →','tour-next'):link('Try the work →','assessment','primary')}</div>${link('Back to roles','discovery')}</div></div>`,'Discover')}
function practice(){return shell(`${title('Practise the work.','Use the role you chose to turn understanding into action.',true)}${hero('Available now · 15 minutes','Try a shift.<br><em>See what to strengthen.</em>','Handle a connected workplace scenario through decisions, priorities, messages and a short update.',link('Open your work shift →','assessment','primary'),'<div class="message" style="background:#073c3433;border-color:#ffffff30;color:#e9f6ef"><strong style="color:#b9e4d0">ONE SCENARIO</strong>A delayed delivery.<br>A waiting customer.<br>Your next decision.</div>')}<div class="grid3">${panel('Your assessment feedback','Return to the evidence and your next improvement.',link('Review feedback →','result'))}${panel('Interview answers','Practise putting your experience into words.',link('Practise one answer →','questions'))}${panel('Your past attempts','See what you worked through, by role.',link('Open past results →','history'))}</div>${section('Still in development')}<div class="split equal">${panel('Role missions','More workplace practice is planned.',link('View availability','missions'),'soft')}${panel('Career Passport','A shareable evidence record is planned.',link('View availability','passport'),'soft')}</div>`,'Practice')}
const moments=[['Choose your first action','A customer asks whether their delayed parcel will arrive before 5 pm. Dispatch has not confirmed an arrival time.'],['Set the team’s priorities','You have a waiting customer, an unresolved dispatch check and routine case notes. Put the work in the order you would handle it.'],['Leave a clear handover','A colleague will take over the case. Give them enough information to continue without asking you to repeat it.'],['Give the customer an update','Dispatch now expects arrival after 5 pm. Explain the change and the next step you can actually offer.']];
function responseUI(format,admin=false){if(format==='Decision cards')return `<div class="decision">${['Check the delivery status with dispatch','Promise it will arrive before 5 pm','Close the case and wait for another call'].map((s,i)=>button(s,admin?'admin-card':'decision','',`data-value="${i}" aria-pressed="${!admin&&state.assessmentAnswers[0]===i}"`)).join('')}</div>`;if(format==='Prioritise')return `<div id="priority-list">${(state.assessmentAnswers.priority||['Check the delivery estimate','Update the waiting customer','Complete routine case notes']).map(s=>`<div class="priorityitem"><span>${s}</span><div>${button('↑','move-up','',`aria-label="Move ${s} up"`)}${button('↓','move-down','',`aria-label="Move ${s} down"`)}</div></div>`).join('')}</div>`;if(format==='Handover')return `<div class="stack"><label>Current status<input data-answer="status" placeholder="What is confirmed?" value="${esc(state.assessmentAnswers.status||'')}"></label><label>Next owner<input data-answer="owner" placeholder="Who takes over?" value="${esc(state.assessmentAnswers.owner||'')}"></label><label>Next action<textarea data-answer="action" placeholder="What should they do, and by when?">${esc(state.assessmentAnswers.action||'')}</textarea></label></div>`;return `<div class="chips">${button('Type the update','update-mode','', 'aria-pressed="true"')}${button('Record an update','record-demo','', 'aria-pressed="false"')}</div><label>Your customer update<textarea data-answer="update" placeholder="Say what changed, acknowledge the impact and explain the next step.">${esc(state.assessmentAnswers.update||'')}</textarea></label><small>Recording is simulated in this preview. No microphone is accessed.</small>`}
function assessment(){if(!state.assessmentStarted)return shell(`${title('A short shift in customer success.','Try the work before worrying about a score.')}<div class="split"><div class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">Your scenario</span><h2>A delivery is late.<br>The customer needs a clear answer.</h2><p>You will decide what to do, order the priorities, leave a handover and give an update.</p><div class="chips">${badge('15 minutes total','guide')}${badge('Work saved as you go')}${badge('Feedback after the shift')}</div><div class="notice">The timer starts when you press Start. It keeps running if you leave the page. At 15 minutes, your saved work is submitted.</div><div class="actions">${button('Start 15-minute shift →','assessment-start')}</div><small>Preview rehearsal: the clock is illustrative; no attempt is created.</small></div><aside class="stack">${panel('Know what to expect','Try a response format before the timer starts.',button('Try a sample decision','rehearse','secondary'))}${panel('Already tried this role?','Revisit the feedback before taking it again.',link('Review last feedback →','result'))}</aside></div>`,'Practice');if(state.assessmentReview)return shell(`${title('Your shift is complete.','Review the responses you tried in this preview.')}<div class="panel"><div class="row"><div><strong>First decision</strong><small>${state.assessmentAnswers[0]===undefined?'No decision selected':['Check dispatch','Promise arrival','Close the case'][state.assessmentAnswers[0]]}</small></div>${badge('Preview response')}</div><div class="row"><div><strong>Priorities</strong><small>${esc((state.assessmentAnswers.priority||['Check the delivery estimate','Update the waiting customer','Complete routine case notes']).join(' → '))}</small></div></div><div class="row"><div><strong>Handover</strong><small>${esc(state.assessmentAnswers.status||'No status entered')} · ${esc(state.assessmentAnswers.owner||'No owner entered')} · ${esc(state.assessmentAnswers.action||'No action entered')}</small></div></div><div class="row"><div><strong>Customer update</strong><small>${esc(state.assessmentAnswers.update||'No update entered')}</small></div></div><div class="actions">${link('See the feedback concept →','result','primary')}${button('Try the rehearsal again','assessment-reset','secondary')}</div></div>`,'Practice');const i=state.assessmentMoment;return shell(`<div class="workspacebar"><div><span class="eyebrow">Customer success · work shift</span><h2>${moments[i][0]}</h2></div><div class="timer">15:00<small>Illustrative preview clock</small></div></div><div class="split"><aside class="panel soft"><span class="eyebrow">The situation</span><div class="message"><strong>Customer case · delayed delivery</strong>${moments[i][1]}</div><details><summary>Check the case facts</summary><p>The customer needs the parcel by 5 pm. You can check dispatch and explain confirmed information. You cannot guarantee a delivery time you have not verified.</p></details><p class="note">Your decisions stay in this preview.</p></aside><section class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">${['Decision','Priorities','Handover','Customer update'][i]}</span>${responseUI(['Decision cards','Prioritise','Handover','Spoken update'][i])}<div class="actions">${button(i===3?'Finish rehearsal →':'Continue →','assessment-next')}${i>0?button('Back','assessment-back','secondary'):''}</div><p id="response-status" class="note" role="status"></p></section></div>`,'Practice')}
function result(){return shell(`${title('Make the next step clear.','Assessment feedback concept · illustrative evidence, not a new score.',true)}<div class="split"><div><div class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">What your work showed</span><h2>You checked the facts.<br>Now make the handover actionable.</h2><p>Keep the customer update honest. Before handing the case over, name the next owner and when they should act.</p><div class="actions">${link('Practise a clear update →','questions','primary')}</div></div>${section('The evidence behind the feedback')}<div class="panel"><div class="row"><div><strong>Checking before promising</strong><small>The selected action asks dispatch for a confirmed estimate.</small></div>${badge('Shown in this task','earned')}</div><div class="row"><div><strong>Leaving a usable handover</strong><small>Name an owner and a time for the next update.</small></div>${badge('Next focus','guide')}</div><details><summary>Review the response and feedback</summary><div class="message"><strong>Example response</strong>“Dispatch is checking the estimate. The customer needs an update.”</div><p>What to add: who will contact the customer, and when. A useful handover lets the next person act without reconstructing the case.</p></details></div></div><aside class="stack">${panel('How to read this','This feedback speaks for the tasks attempted. Unattempted skills are not a low score. No employer threshold or future improvement is assumed.')}<div class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">Example coverage</span><h3>Completed tasks, named clearly</h3><div class="row"><span class="smallcopy">Decision</span>${badge('Completed','earned')}</div><div class="row"><span class="smallcopy">Handover</span>${badge('Needs detail','guide')}</div>${link('View past assessments →','history')}</div></aside></div>`,'Practice')}
function history(){return shell(`${title('Your past assessments','Keep the role and the work covered beside each result.')}<div class="panel"><label>Role<select id="history-role"><option>All roles</option><option ${state.historyRole==='Customer Success Associate'?'selected':''}>Customer Success Associate</option><option ${state.historyRole==='Operations Coordinator'?'selected':''}>Operations Coordinator</option></select></label><p class="note">Illustrative history. Actual records would show their saved dates and scores.</p>${['Customer Success Associate','Customer Success Associate','Operations Coordinator'].filter(r=>state.historyRole==='All roles'||state.historyRole===r).map((r,i)=>`<article class="historyentry"><div><span class="eyebrow">${i===0?'Most recent example':'Earlier example'}</span><h3>${r}</h3><p>${i===1?'Some situations not completed':'Decisions and handover reviewed'}</p>${badge(i===1?'Partial attempt':'Completed attempt',i===1?'planned':'earned')}</div>${link('Review this assessment →','result','secondary')}</article>`).join('')}</div><p class="note">Compare progress only when the role, assessment version and coverage make the comparison meaningful.</p>`,'Practice')}
function interviews(){return shell(`${title('Prepare for the conversation.','Choose the amount of practice you need today.',true)}${hero('Start small','One question.<br><em>A clearer answer.</em>','Try explaining a real experience, get one useful note and try again.',link('Practise one question →','questions','primary'))}<div class="split equal">${panel('A full interview','A ten-minute conversation for your chosen role. Speak or type.',link('Set up an interview →','interview','secondary'))}${panel('Your previous interviews','Return to the feedback and transcript before starting another.',button('See saved-session concept','interview-history','secondary'))}</div>${section('A future part of your preparation')}${panel('Story bank','A place to keep examples from your experience. Not released yet.',link('View availability','stories'),'soft')}`,'Practice')}
function interview(){if(state.interviewStarted)return shell(`<div class="workspacebar"><div><span class="eyebrow">Customer Success Associate · rehearsal</span><h2>Take a moment. Then answer.</h2></div><div class="timer">10:00<small>Illustrative preview clock</small></div></div><div class="split"><div class="interviewer"><div class="orb" aria-hidden="true">A</div><p>Asha · practice interviewer</p><div class="wave" aria-hidden="true">${'<i></i>'.repeat(9)}</div><small style="color:#b9dfce">${state.interviewMode==='Type'?'Written answers':'Voice mode concept · no recording'}</small></div><div class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">Your question</span><h2 style="font-size:24px">${questions[state.interviewQuestion%questions.length]}</h2><label>Your answer<textarea id="interview-answer" placeholder="Use a real example: what happened, what you did, and the result.">${esc(state.interviewAnswers[state.interviewQuestion]||'')}</textarea></label><div class="actions">${button('Continue →','interview-next')}${button('Finish rehearsal','interview-finish','secondary')}</div><small>Preview only. Nothing is recorded, submitted or scored.</small></div></div>`,'Practice');return shell(`${title('Ready for a short practice interview?','Ten minutes. Your chosen role. Feedback on the answers you give.')}<div class="split"><div class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">How would you like to answer?</span><div class="chips">${['Type','Speak'].map(t=>button(t,'interview-mode','',`data-value="${t}" aria-pressed="${state.interviewMode===t}"`)).join('')}</div>${state.interviewMode==='Speak'?`<div class="notice">Check your microphone before starting. This preview demonstrates the check without recording.</div>${button('Try microphone check','mic-check','textlink')}`:'<p class="smallcopy">No microphone needed. Type each answer at your own pace within the session.</p>'}<label>Role<input value="Customer Success Associate" readonly></label><div class="sectiontitle"><h3>Focus for this session</h3></div><p>Ground your answer in one specific experience.</p><details><summary>Round, interviewer and other settings</summary><div class="fieldgrid"><label>Round<select><option>HR round</option><option>Managerial round</option></select></label><label>Interviewer<select><option>Asha</option><option>Ravi</option></select></label></div><label>Anything else to practise? <small>Optional</small><input placeholder="Add a focus"></label></details><div class="actions">${button('Start 10-minute interview →','interview-start')}</div><small>Opens a local rehearsal; no AI generation.</small></div><aside class="interviewer"><div class="orb" aria-hidden="true">A</div><p>A quiet place to try, reflect and try again.</p></aside></div>`,'Practice')}
function questionPractice(){return shell(`${title('Make one answer stronger.','A short practice space for the questions interviews ask.')}<div class="split"><section class="panel"><div class="row"><span class="eyebrow">${state.question===0?'Learning quickly':'Communicating clearly'}</span>${badge(state.questionFeedback?'Feedback example':'Try this question','guide')}</div><h2 style="font-size:25px">${questions[state.question%questions.length]}</h2>${state.questionFeedback?`<div class="callout"><h3>Add the moment, not just the skill.</h3><p>Choose one situation. Say what you did to learn, and how you checked it worked.</p></div><details open><summary>Your draft</summary><p>${esc(state.questionAnswer||'No draft entered.')}</p></details><div class="actions">${button('Improve my answer','question-retry')}${button('Next question →','question-next','secondary')}</div><p class="note">This is fixed example coaching, not an AI assessment of your answer.</p>`:`<label>Your answer<textarea id="question-answer" placeholder="What happened? What did you do? What changed?">${esc(state.questionAnswer||'')}</textarea></label><details><summary>Need a starting point?</summary><p>“When I was …, I needed to learn … . I started by … and checked my work by … .” Use your own experience.</p></details><div class="actions">${button('Review feedback →','question-feedback')}</div>`}</section><aside class="panel soft"><h3>Find another question</h3><label class="sr" for="question-search">Search questions</label><input id="question-search" type="search" placeholder="Search questions…"><div id="question-options">${questions.map((q,i)=>`<div class="row question-option" data-question="${esc(q.toLowerCase())}">${button(q,'question-pick','textlink',`data-value="${i}"`)}</div>`).join('')}</div><p class="note">Practice is a place to improve. A previous attempt is a starting point.</p></aside></div>`,'Practice')}
function unavailable(kind){const cfg={stories:['Your story bank is on the way.','Keep practising the examples you would use in an interview.','The story bank is not released yet. It will not unlock by completing another task today.','Practise an interview answer →','questions'],missions:['More workplace practice is on the way.','Role missions are still in development.','You can use the available assessment to try the work, or practise an interview answer now.','Open the work shift →','assessment'],passport:['Your evidence deserves a clear record.','The Career Passport is not released yet.','Your existing assessment results are available now. You do not need to repeat an assessment to unlock this page.','Open your assessment results →','history'],opportunities:['Found a job you like?','Employer matching is not available in Ascend yet.','While we build the network, use a real posting you have found to see which requirements your record supports.','Check a job description →','jobfit']}[kind];return shell(`${title(cfg[0],cfg[1])}<div class="split"><div class="panel">${badge('Not released yet','planned')}<h2 style="margin-top:23px">${kind==='opportunities'?'Work with the tools available today.':'Your progress is not the blocker.'}</h2><p>${cfg[2]}</p><div class="actions">${link(cfg[3],cfg[4],'primary')}</div></div><aside class="panel soft"><span class="eyebrow">Planned experience · illustration only</span>${kind==='passport'?`<div class="fileart">CAREER PASSPORT<b>Your work.<br>Your evidence.</b><span></span><span></span></div><p>No passport is issued or shared in this preview.</p>`:kind==='stories'?`<h3>A story from your experience</h3><div class="row"><strong>Situation</strong><small>The real moment</small></div><div class="row"><strong>Action</strong><small>What you did</small></div><div class="row"><strong>Result</strong><small>What changed</small></div>`:kind==='missions'?`<div class="tourblank" style="height:200px"><div class="desk"></div></div><p>Role-specific practice, when the module is ready.</p>`:`<h3>A future talent network</h3><p>Role requirements linked to the work a candidate has demonstrated.</p><p>No jobs or employers are fabricated for this preview.</p>`}</aside></div>`,kind==='opportunities'?'Opportunities':'Practice')}
function presence(){return shell(`${title('Prepare to put yourself forward.','Your resume, LinkedIn profile and fit for a specific job.',true)}${hero('Continue your work','Make your experience<br><em>easy to understand.</em>','Open your latest resume, check the facts and make it ready for the role.',link('Continue your resume →','resume','primary'))}<div class="grid3">${panel('Resume Builder','Edit your document and check it before downloading.',link('Open Resume Builder →','resume'))}${panel('LinkedIn Profile Builder','Review and copy one section at a time.',link('Open LinkedIn builder →','linkedin'))}${panel('Job Fit Analyzer','Compare a job description with your evidence.',link('Check a job →','jobfit'))}</div><p class="note">Illustrative returning-user state. A new student would see Create a resume as the first action.</p>`)}
function resume(){return shell(`${title('Your resume','Customer Success Associate · illustrative saved document')}<div class="workspacebar"><div class="sectionnav" style="margin:0;border:0">${['Edit','Review','Download'].map(t=>button(t,'resume-tab','',`data-value="${t}" aria-pressed="${t===state.resumeTab}"`)).join('')}</div>${button('Saved documents','resume-history','secondary')}</div><div class="split"><div class="panel">${state.resumeTab==='Edit'?`<h3>Use your facts. Keep your voice.</h3><p>Change a section and see it in the document beside you.</p><label>Name<input id="resume-name" value="${esc(state.resumeName)}"></label><label>Summary<textarea id="resume-summary">${esc(state.resumeSummary||'Commerce graduate exploring customer success, with a college help-desk project and experience coordinating student queries.')}</textarea></label><label>Layout<select id="resume-layout">${['Classic','Compact','Sidebar'].map(t=>`<option ${state.resumeLayout===t?'selected':''}>${t}</option>`).join('')}</select><div class="actions">${button('Save preview changes','resume-save')}</div><details><summary>Help me improve a section</summary><p>In the live tool, suggestions should use your existing facts and let you review the changes before keeping them.</p>${button('See a suggested edit','resume-suggest','secondary')}</details>`:state.resumeTab==='Review'?`<h3>Check before you download.</h3><div class="row"><div><strong>Names, dates and contact details</strong><small>Confirm these against your own record.</small></div></div><div class="row"><div><strong>What you did</strong><small>Keep only statements you can explain.</small></div></div><div class="row"><div><strong>Readable layout</strong><small>Classic and Compact use one column.</small></div></div>${button('Ready to download →','resume-ready')}`:`<h3>Your document, ready to take with you.</h3><p>The live builder supports document exports. This concept keeps export actions next to the reviewed version.</p><div class="actions">${button('Preview PDF export','export-preview')}${button('Preview Word export','export-preview','secondary')}</div><p class="note">No file is generated by these demonstration controls.</p>`}</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Example document · not your saved resume</span><article class="document ${state.resumeLayout.toLowerCase()}" id="resume-document"><h2 id="document-name">${esc(state.resumeName)}</h2><small>Customer Success Associate · sample contact details</small><h3>Summary</h3><p id="document-summary">${esc(state.resumeSummary||'Commerce graduate exploring customer success, with a college help-desk project and experience coordinating student queries.')}</p><h3>Experience & projects</h3><p>Student help desk · College project · Example experience</p><p>Organised incoming student queries, recorded follow-up notes and passed unresolved questions to the right team.</p><h3>Education</h3><p>B.Com · Example college · 2026</p><h3>Skills</h3><p>Written communication · Case notes · Google Sheets</p></article></div></div>`)}
const linkedinSections=[['Headline','Aspiring Customer Success Associate | Customer communication & problem-solving'],['About','I am exploring customer success roles where I can help people understand their next step. I am building practical experience in communication, case notes and handovers.'],['Skills','Customer communication · Case documentation · Team coordination']];
function linkedin(){return shell(`${title('LinkedIn Profile Builder','Review a section, keep what is accurate, then copy it into LinkedIn.')}<div class="notice">Saved in Ascend and published on LinkedIn are different steps. Nothing here updates LinkedIn automatically.</div><div class="split" style="margin-top:22px"><div class="stack">${linkedinSections.map(([h,v],i)=>`<section class="copycard"><div class="row"><h3 style="margin:0">${h}</h3>${badge(state.linkedinSaved[i]?'Saved in preview':'Example draft',state.linkedinSaved[i]?'earned':'guide')}</div><label class="sr" for="linkedin-${i}">${h}</label><textarea id="linkedin-${i}" rows="${i===1?5:2}">${esc(state['linkedinValue'+i]||v)}</textarea><div class="actions">${button('Save section','linkedin-save','primary',`data-value="${i}"`)}${button('Copy for LinkedIn','linkedin-copy','secondary',`data-value="${i}"`)}${button('Suggest an edit','linkedin-suggest','textlink',`data-value="${i}"`)}</div></section>`).join('')}</div><aside class="panel soft"><span class="eyebrow">Example profile</span><div class="avatar" style="width:64px;height:64px;margin:15px 0">A</div><h2 style="font-size:22px">Sample student</h2><p>A profile should read like the same person as the resume.</p><details><summary>What should I check?</summary><p>Check every claim against your own experience. Save the section in Ascend when it is accurate, then copy it across yourself.</p></details></aside></div>`)}
function jobfit(){return shell(`${title(state.jobResult?'See where your evidence fits.':'Is this job a useful next step?',state.jobResult?'Illustrative analysis layout. No posting was analysed.':'Paste the responsibilities and requirements from a real job posting.')} ${state.jobResult?`<div class="split"><div class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">Requirement → evidence → action</span><div class="row"><div><strong>Clear customer communication</strong><small>Link to a relevant practice answer or work example.</small></div>${badge('Evidence to review','earned')}</div><div class="row"><div><strong>Using a CRM</strong><small>No supporting example in this illustration.</small></div>${badge('Not demonstrated','guide')}</div><div class="row"><div><strong>Reliable handovers</strong><small>Add an example that names the status, owner and next step.</small></div>${link('Practise →','assessment')}</div><details><summary>See the posting you entered</summary><p>${esc(state.jobText||'Example job description')}</p></details></div><aside class="panel soft"><h3>Before you apply</h3><p>Check the missing evidence. “Not demonstrated” means the record does not show it; it is not a judgement that you cannot do it.</p>${link('Review your resume →','resume','primary')}<div class="actions">${button('Check another posting','job-reset','textlink')}</div></aside></div>`:`<div class="split"><form id="job-form" class="panel"><label>Job description<textarea id="job-description" rows="10" required minlength="80" placeholder="Paste the role responsibilities and requirements here…">${esc(state.jobText||'')}</textarea></label><p class="note">Include the full description. A job title alone cannot show the requirements.</p><div class="actions"><button class="primary" type="submit">Check my fit →</button>${button('Use a sample posting','job-sample','textlink')}</div><p id="job-error" class="note" role="status"></p></form><aside class="panel soft"><h3>What you will be able to decide</h3><p>Which requirements your work supports, which need more evidence, and what to improve before applying.</p><details><summary>What would Ascend use?</summary><p>Your profile and completed work. A missing piece of evidence should be stated, never turned into a made-up match percentage.</p></details></aside></div>`}`)}
function journey(){return shell(`${title('Your journey, with a clear next step.','Progress you make is separate from features we are still building.',true)}<div class="split"><section class="panel"><ol class="journeyline"><li class="done"><strong>Choose your direction</strong><p>Customer Success Associate</p>${link('Revisit the workplace','tour')}</li><li class="now"><strong>Try the work</strong><p>Use a 15-minute assessment to see what to strengthen.</p>${link('Open your work shift →','assessment','primary')}</li><li><strong>Practise the conversation</strong><p>One answer at a time, or a ten-minute interview.</p>${link('Open interview practice','interviews')}</li><li><strong>Prepare your application</strong><p>Build your resume and LinkedIn profile from your experience.</p>${link('Open your application tools','presence')}</li></ol></section><aside class="stack">${panel('Your saved work','Results and documents remain available as you progress.',link('Past assessments →','history'))}<div class="panel soft">${badge('Still in development','planned')}<h3 style="margin-top:18px">Missions, Passport & opportunities</h3><p>These are product releases, not incomplete tasks on your personal checklist.</p>${link('See what you can do now →','practice')}</div></aside></div>`)}
function settings(){return shell(`${title('Settings','Your account, appearance and data.')}<div class="split"><div class="stack"><section class="panel"><h3>Appearance</h3><p>Choose the theme that feels comfortable.</p><div class="chips">${['Light','Dark'].map(t=>button(t,'settings-theme','',`data-value="${t.toLowerCase()}" aria-pressed="${document.documentElement.dataset.theme===t.toLowerCase()}"`)).join('')}</div></section>${panel('Account','You are viewing a sample account.',link('Switch account →','auth','secondary'))}${panel('Your profile','Update your background and preferences.',link('Edit profile →','profile','secondary'))}</div><aside class="panel soft"><h3>Your data</h3><p>Deletion belongs here, separate from everyday preferences.</p><details><summary>Delete profile</summary><p>In the live product, this deletes saved profile data and activity and signs you out. A deliberate confirmation must remain.</p>${button('See confirmation design','delete-design','secondary')}</details></aside></div>`)}
function cohort(kind){const college=kind==='college';return shell(`${hero(college?'For colleges · pilot access':'For employers · pilot access',college?'Help your cohort<br><em>prepare for the work.</em>':'See capability<br><em>before the first day.</em>',college?'Connect role exploration, practical preparation and evidence of readiness. College dashboards are planned.':'Connect role requirements to demonstrated work. Employer screening tools are planned.',button('Prepare an access request →','cohort-focus','primary'),college?'<div class="cohortart" aria-hidden="true"><div></div><div></div><div></div><div></div></div>':fileart())}<div class="split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Planned workflow · illustration</span><div class="panel"><ol class="journeyline">${(college?[['Understand the cohort','See where students are in their preparation.'],['Focus your support','Connect gaps to useful practice.'],['Show the evidence','Review the work behind readiness.']]:[['Define the role','Name the work a new hire needs to do.'],['Review relevant evidence','See how candidates handled related tasks.'],['Make a more informed choice','Use the evidence in your hiring conversation.']]).map(([h,p])=>`<li><strong>${h}</strong><p>${p}</p></li>`).join('')}</ol></div><p class="note">These capabilities are not released. No cohort outcomes or candidate scores are claimed here.</p></div><form id="cohort-form" class="panel"><h3>Prepare an access request</h3><p>Opens an email draft for you to send. This preview only shows the draft.</p><div class="stack"><label>${college?'College':'Company'}<input name="org" required placeholder="${college?'Your college':'Your company'}"></label><label>Your name<input name="name" required></label><label>Work email<input name="email" type="email" required></label><label>Your role<input name="role" required placeholder="${college?'e.g. Placement officer':'e.g. Talent acquisition lead'}"></label></div><div class="actions"><button class="primary" type="submit">Prepare email draft →</button></div><small>No request is sent from this preview.</small></form></div>`,college?'College':'Employer')}
function auth(){return shell(`<div class="authscreen"><span class="eyebrow">Return to Resume Builder</span><h2>Keep your work with you.</h2><p>Sign in to save your resume and pick up where you left off.</p>${button('Continue with Google','auth-google','secondary')}<details><summary>Use email instead</summary><form id="auth-form"><label>Email<input type="email" required placeholder="you@example.com"></label><label>Password<input type="password" required minlength="8" autocomplete="off"></label><div class="actions"><button class="primary" type="submit">Sign in and continue →</button></div></form></details><p class="note">New to Ascend? ${button('Create an account','auth-signup','textlink')}</p>${link('Continue exploring','home')}<p class="note">Design preview. No sign-in request is made.</p></div>`)}
function admin(){const tabs=['Scenario','Skills','Response','Student preview','Publish'];return shell(`${title('Build a role experience.','Keep the role, assessment and student view together.')}<div class="adminlayout"><aside class="panel adminroles">${roles.map(([r])=>button(r,'admin-role','',`data-value="${r}" aria-pressed="${r===state.adminRole}"`)).join('')}</aside><section><div class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">${state.adminRole} · draft example</span><div class="sectionnav">${tabs.map(t=>button(t,'admin-tab','',`data-value="${t}" aria-pressed="${t===state.adminTab}"`)).join('')}</div>${state.adminTab==='Scenario'?`<label>Scenario title<input value="A delivery is late"></label><label>What does the student need to know?<textarea>A customer needs a parcel by 5 pm. Dispatch has not confirmed an arrival time. The student must decide what to check and what to communicate.</textarea></label><details><summary>Role details, interview questions & media</summary><p>Keep existing authoring capabilities reachable under this role, with their own draft and published states.</p><div class="actions">${button('Role details','admin-details','secondary')}${button('Interview questions','admin-questions','secondary')}${button('Media library','admin-media','secondary')}</div></details>`:state.adminTab==='Skills'?`<h3>What will this situation show?</h3><div class="chips">${['Communication','Prioritisation','Record keeping','Judgement'].map(t=>button(t,'interest','', 'aria-pressed="true"')).join('')}</div><label>What does a good response demonstrate?<textarea>Checks what is confirmed, stays within authority and leaves a usable next step.</textarea></label><p class="note">Skill mapping and scoring remain authored in the backend. This is an editing layout.</p>`:state.adminTab==='Response'?`<label>Response format<select id="admin-format">${['Decision cards','Prioritise','Handover','Spoken update'].map(t=>`<option ${state.adminFormat===t?'selected':''}>${t}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><p class="note">Different moments in one assessment can use different formats.</p>${responseUI(state.adminFormat,true)}`:state.adminTab==='Student preview'?`<div class="workspacebar"><div><span class="eyebrow">Student view</span><h3>Choose your first action</h3></div><div class="timer">15:00<small>Total assessment limit</small></div></div><div class="message"><strong>Customer case</strong>A customer asks whether their parcel will arrive before 5 pm. The arrival time is not confirmed.</div><div style="margin-top:18px">${responseUI(state.adminFormat,true)}</div>`:`<h3>Review the draft before publishing.</h3><div class="row"><strong>Role and scenario</strong>${badge('Review')}</div><div class="row"><strong>Skills and evidence criteria</strong>${badge('Review')}</div><div class="row"><strong>Response formats and media</strong>${badge('Review')}</div><div class="row"><strong>Total time limit</strong>${badge('15 minutes','guide')}</div><p class="note">Publishing should state exactly which draft students will see. This preview cannot publish.</p>${button('Preview publication confirmation','admin-publish','secondary')}`}</div><footer class="adminfooter"><p id="admin-status">${state.adminSaved?'Draft saved in preview only':'Draft changes · not visible to students'}</p><div class="actions" style="margin:0">${button('Save draft','admin-save','secondary')}${button('Review as student →','admin-preview')}</div></footer></section></div>`)}
function welcome(){return `<div class="locknote">Welcome revision: choose the realistic animation theme. <a href="/previews/ascend-film-storyboard.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the timed one-minute storyboard ↗</a></div><iframe class="welcomeembed" title="Ascend realistic animation theme review" src="/previews/ascend-animation-themes.html" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-top-navigation-by-user-activation"></iframe><div class="screen" style="min-height:auto">${section('Connected destinations')}<div class="grid3">${panel('Students','Explore, prepare and show your work.',link('Student home →','home'))}${panel('Colleges','Focus preparation across a cohort.',link('College home →','college'))}${panel('Employers','Connect hiring to demonstrated capability.',link('Employer home →','employer'))}</div></div>`}
const renderers={overview,welcome,auth,home,profile,discovery,tour,practice,assessment,result,history,interviews,interview,questions:questionPractice,stories:()=>unavailable('stories'),missions:()=>unavailable('missions'),presence,resume,linkedin,jobfit,journey,passport:()=>unavailable('passport'),opportunities:()=>unavailable('opportunities'),settings,college:()=>cohort('college'),employer:()=>cohort('employer'),admin};
function toast(message){$('#toast').textContent=message;$('#toast').style.display='block';clearTimeout(toast.timer);toast.timer=setTimeout(()=>$('#toast').style.display='none',4500)}
function modal(html){$('#dialog-body').innerHTML=html;$('#detail-dialog').showModal()}
function notes(p){const publicOnly=['journey','opportunities','missions','college','employer','auth','welcome','interviews','settings','tour'].includes(p.id);return `<div><h2>FRICTION IN THE CURRENT EXPERIENCE</h2><p>${p.friction}</p></div><div><h2>WHAT THIS PREVIEW CHANGES</h2><p>${p.proposal}</p></div><div class="evidence">${p.id==='overview'?'Review coverage':publicOnly?'Public browser + source review':'Signed-in page observed + source review'} · Live save, generation and publishing flows are not certified. ${['stories','missions','passport','opportunities','college','employer'].includes(p.id)?'Feature availability is preserved; this does not release the planned product.':''}</div>`}
function nav(){let group='';const query=$('#find-page').value.toLowerCase();$('#page-list').innerHTML=pages.filter(p=>(p.title+' '+p.group).toLowerCase().includes(query)).map(p=>{const h=group===p.group?'':`<span class="navgroup">${p.group}</span>`;group=p.group;return h+`<a href="#${p.id}" ${p.id===state.page?'aria-current="page"':''}>${p.title}</a>`}).join('')}
function render(focus=false){const p=pages.find(p=>p.id===state.page)||pages[0];$('#page-title').textContent=p.id==='overview'?'A clearer path to productive work.':p.title;$('#group-label').textContent=p.group;$('#current-link').href=p.path;$('#current-link').hidden=p.id==='overview';$('#review-notes').innerHTML=notes(p);$('#review-notes').hidden=!state.notes;$('#preview').innerHTML=renderers[p.id]();if(p.id==='profile'){const vals=state.profileDrafts?.[state.profileTab];if(vals)document.querySelectorAll('#preview input,#preview textarea,#preview select').forEach((e,i)=>{if(vals[i]!==undefined)e.value=vals[i]})}if(p.id==='admin'){const vals=state.adminDrafts?.[state.adminRole+'|'+state.adminTab];if(vals)document.querySelectorAll('#preview input,#preview textarea').forEach((e,i)=>{if(vals[i]!==undefined)e.value=vals[i]})}nav();if(focus)$('#preview').focus({preventScroll:true});document.title=`Ascend preview · ${p.title}`}
function go(){state.page=pages.some(p=>p.id===location.hash.slice(1))?location.hash.slice(1):'overview';render();window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'instant'})}
function setTheme(theme){document.documentElement.dataset.theme=theme;$('#theme').textContent=theme==='dark'?'Light theme':'Dark theme';try{localStorage.setItem('ascend:review-theme',theme)}catch{}}
function keepInputs(){if(state.page==='profile'){state.profileDrafts??={};state.profileDrafts[state.profileTab]=[...document.querySelectorAll('#preview input,#preview textarea,#preview select')].map(e=>e.value)}if(state.page==='admin'){state.adminDrafts??={};state.adminDrafts[state.adminRole+'|'+state.adminTab]=[...document.querySelectorAll('#preview input,#preview textarea')].map(e=>e.value)}if($('#question-answer'))state.questionAnswer=$('#question-answer').value;if($('#interview-answer'))state.interviewAnswers[state.interviewQuestion]=$('#interview-answer').value;for(let i=0;i<3;i++)if($('#linkedin-'+i))state['linkedinValue'+i]=$('#linkedin-'+i).value}
const samplePosting='Customer Success Associate. Help customers resolve delivery queries, keep accurate case notes, coordinate with operations and follow up on unresolved cases. Requirements: clear written communication, spreadsheet skills, reliable handovers and a willingness to learn a CRM.';
document.addEventListener('click',async e=>{const el=e.target.closest('[data-action]');if(!el)return;const a=el.dataset.action,v=el.dataset.value;keepInputs();switch(a){
case'profile-tab':state.profileTab=v;state.profileSaved=false;render();break;
case'profile-save':state.profileSaved=true;$('#profile-status').textContent='Saved in this preview';toast('Section saved in the preview only.');break;
case'profile-import':modal(`<span class="eyebrow">Import review concept</span><h2>Check what was found.</h2><p>Keep the source and each imported fact together before updating the profile.</p><div class="row"><strong>Name</strong>${badge('Review imported value')}</div><div class="row"><strong>Education</strong>${badge('Review imported entries')}</div><div class="row"><strong>Experience</strong>${badge('Review dates and role')}</div><p>No file is uploaded in this concept.</p>`);break;
case'interest':el.setAttribute('aria-pressed',el.getAttribute('aria-pressed')!=='true');break;
case'industries':modal(`<h2>What interests you?</h2><p>Use these choices to order the roles. You can still explore everything.</p><div class="chips">${['Customer service','Retail','Logistics','Banking'].map(t=>button(t,'interest','', 'aria-pressed="false"')).join('')}</div>${button('Keep exploring','close-dialog')}`);break;
case'role-detail':{const r=roles[Number(v)];modal(`<span class="eyebrow">${r[1]}</span><h2>${r[0]}</h2><p>${r[2]}</p><div class="row"><strong>Day-to-day work</strong><span class="smallcopy">${r[3]}</span></div><p>Explore the workplace before choosing this direction. This concept does not change your saved role.</p><div class="actions">${link('Step into the workplace →','tour','primary')}${button('Choose in this preview','choose-role','secondary',`data-value="${v}"`)}</div>`);break}
case'choose-role':toast(roles[Number(v)][0]+' selected in this concept only.');$('#detail-dialog').close();break;
case'compare':modal(`<h2>Compare the work.</h2><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Core work</th><th>Workplace</th></tr></thead><tbody>${state.compare.map(i=>`<tr><td>${roles[i][0]}</td><td>${roles[i][2]}</td><td>${roles[i][3]}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p class="note">Pay and entry requirements should come from the published role details, with sources. They are not invented for this preview.</p>${link('See the workplace →','tour','primary')}`);break;
case'tour-play':state.tourOn=!state.tourOn;render();break;
case'tour-stop':state.tourStop=Number(v);render();break;
case'tour-next':state.tourStop++;render();break;
case'rehearse':modal(`<span class="eyebrow">Untimed sample</span><h2>What would you check first?</h2><p>A customer needs a confirmed arrival time. Dispatch has not provided one.</p>${responseUI('Decision cards',true)}<p class="note">The timed assessment has not started.</p>`);break;
case'admin-card':el.parentElement.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===el)));break;
case'assessment-start':state.assessmentStarted=true;render(true);break;
case'decision':state.assessmentAnswers[0]=Number(v);el.parentElement.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===el)));break;
case'assessment-next':if(state.assessmentMoment===0&&state.assessmentAnswers[0]===undefined){$('#response-status').textContent='Choose an action to continue.';break}if(state.assessmentMoment===2&&(!state.assessmentAnswers.status?.trim()||!state.assessmentAnswers.owner?.trim()||!state.assessmentAnswers.action?.trim())){$('#response-status').textContent='Add the status, next owner and action.';break}if(state.assessmentMoment===3&&!state.assessmentAnswers.update?.trim()){$('#response-status').textContent='Add your customer update to finish the rehearsal.';break}if(state.assessmentMoment===3)state.assessmentReview=true;else state.assessmentMoment++;render(true);break;
case'assessment-back':state.assessmentMoment--;render();break;
case'assessment-reset':state.assessmentStarted=false;state.assessmentMoment=0;state.assessmentAnswers={};state.assessmentReview=false;render();break;
case'move-up':case'move-down':{const row=el.closest('.priorityitem');const sibling=a==='move-up'?row.previousElementSibling:row.nextElementSibling;if(sibling){if(a==='move-up')sibling.before(row);else sibling.after(row)}state.assessmentAnswers.priority=[...row.parentElement.children].map(n=>n.firstElementChild.textContent);break}
case'update-mode':toast('Type your update below.');break;
case'record-demo':modal('<h2>Record a short update.</h2><p>The live assessment can offer a spoken update with a transcript to review. This design preview does not access your microphone.</p><div class="wave" aria-hidden="true">'+ '<i></i>'.repeat(11)+'</div><p>Recording → review transcript → use response.</p>');break;
case'interview-mode':state.interviewMode=v;render();break;
case'mic-check':toast('Microphone check concept: permission → level check → ready. No audio recorded.');break;
case'interview-start':state.interviewStarted=true;render(true);break;
case'interview-next':if(!state.interviewAnswers[state.interviewQuestion]?.trim()){toast('Add a practice answer before continuing.');break}state.interviewQuestion++;render(true);break;
case'interview-finish':modal(`<h2>Your rehearsal answers</h2><p>In the live interview, feedback should connect to the exact answer. No scoring was run in this preview.</p>${state.interviewAnswers.filter(Boolean).map((x,i)=>`<div class="message"><strong>Answer ${i+1}</strong>${esc(x)}</div>`).join('')||'<p>No answers entered yet.</p>'}${button('Return to setup','interview-reset','secondary')}`);break;
case'interview-reset':state.interviewStarted=false;state.interviewQuestion=0;$('#detail-dialog').close();render();break;
case'interview-history':modal(`<h2>Your interviews, ready to revisit.</h2><p>Each saved session should lead with its role, date and one focus from the feedback.</p><div class="row"><div><strong>Customer Success Associate</strong><small>Example session · focus: specific examples</small></div>${link('Open interview concept →','interview')}</div>`);break;
case'question-pick':state.question=Number(v);state.questionFeedback=false;state.questionAnswer='';render();break;
case'question-feedback':if(!state.questionAnswer?.trim()){toast('Write an answer to try the feedback layout.');break}state.questionFeedback=true;render();break;
case'question-retry':state.questionFeedback=false;render();$('#question-answer').focus();break;
case'question-next':state.question++;state.questionFeedback=false;state.questionAnswer='';render();break;
case'resume-tab':state.resumeTab=v;render();break;
case'resume-ready':state.resumeTab='Download';render();break;
case'resume-save':toast('Saved in the preview. Your Ascend document is unchanged.');break;
case'resume-history':modal(`<h2>Your saved resumes</h2><p>Return to a document without starting a new build.</p><div class="row"><div><strong>Customer Success Associate</strong><small>Illustrative saved version · Classic</small></div>${button('Continue editing','resume-continue','secondary')}</div>${button('Create another version','resume-new','textlink')}`);break;
case'resume-continue':state.resumeTab='Edit';$('#detail-dialog').close();render();break;
case'resume-new':toast('A new version would start from your saved facts, with a separate target role.');break;
case'resume-suggest':modal('<h2>Review the change.</h2><p>Show the original sentence beside the suggestion. Highlight changed words and let the student keep or discard the edit.</p><div class="notice">Never introduce a result, employer or skill that the source record does not support.</div>');break;
case'export-preview':toast('Export placement preview. Use the live Resume Builder for PDF or Word downloads.');break;
case'linkedin-save':state.linkedinSaved[v]=true;render();toast('Section saved in this preview only.');break;
case'linkedin-copy':try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText($('#linkedin-'+v).value);toast('Sample section copied. Paste it yourself; nothing was published.')}catch{toast('Copy is unavailable here. Select and copy the section text.')}break;
case'linkedin-suggest':modal(`<h2>Improve ${linkedinSections[Number(v)][0].toLowerCase()}.</h2><p>Keep editing direct. Offer AI help as an optional action for this section.</p><label>What would you like to change?<textarea placeholder="e.g. Make this shorter while keeping the same facts."></textarea></label>${button('Preview change review','resume-suggest')}`);break;
case'job-sample':state.jobText=samplePosting;$('#job-description').value=samplePosting;break;
case'job-reset':state.jobResult=false;render();break;
case'settings-theme':setTheme(v);render();break;
case'delete-design':modal(`<h2>Delete your profile?</h2><p>The live confirmation should name exactly what will be removed and require a deliberate choice.</p><div class="notice">Preview only. No deletion endpoint is connected.</div><div class="actions">${button('Keep my profile','close-dialog')}${button('Deletion disabled in preview','noop','secondary','disabled')}</div>`);break;
case'cohort-focus':$('#cohort-form').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});$('#cohort-form input').focus({preventScroll:true});break;
case'auth-google':modal(`<h2>Choose your Google account.</h2><p>This concept returns you to Resume Builder after sign-in. The live Google flow should show the account picker.</p>${button('Continue as sample student','auth-demo')}<p class="note">No OAuth request is made from the preview.</p>`);break;
case'auth-demo':$('#detail-dialog').close();location.hash='resume';toast('Demo continuation only. You have not signed in.');break;
case'auth-signup':modal(`<h2>Create an account to keep your work.</h2><p>The same task destination should be preserved when switching between sign-in and account creation.</p>${button('Continue sample flow','auth-demo')}`);break;
case'admin-tab':state.adminTab=v;render();break;
case'admin-role':state.adminRole=v;state.adminSaved=false;render();break;
case'admin-save':state.adminSaved=true;$('#admin-status').textContent='Draft saved in preview only';toast('Preview draft only. Nothing reaches students.');break;
case'admin-preview':state.adminTab='Student preview';render();break;
case'admin-publish':modal(`<span class="eyebrow">Publication review concept</span><h2>Review ${state.adminRole}.</h2><p>The live confirmation should identify the exact draft version, changed scenarios, skill mappings, response formats and assessment duration.</p><div class="notice">Publishing is disabled in this preview.</div>${button('Return to the draft','close-dialog','secondary')}`);break;
case'admin-details':modal('<h2>Role details</h2><p>Keep title, role description, industry variations and workplace tour material under the selected role. Preserve separate draft and published versions.</p>');break;
case'admin-questions':modal('<h2>Interview questions</h2><p>Filter by the selected role and competency. Show the question and student-facing feedback criteria together, with a sample preview before publishing.</p>');break;
case'admin-media':modal('<h2>Media library</h2><p>Show the linked scenario beside each video or image, along with processing state, caption/transcript and replacement controls.</p><div class="notice">Upload and replacement are not connected in this concept.</div>');break;
case'close-dialog':$('#detail-dialog').close();break;
case'copy-request':try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText($('#request-draft').value);toast('Sample email draft copied. Nothing sent.')}catch{toast('Select the draft text and copy it manually.')}break;
}});
document.addEventListener('input',e=>{const t=e.target;if(t.dataset.answer)state.assessmentAnswers[t.dataset.answer]=t.value;if(t.id==='resume-name'){state.resumeName=t.value;$('#document-name').textContent=t.value}if(t.id==='resume-summary'){state.resumeSummary=t.value;$('#document-summary').textContent=t.value}if(t.id==='question-search'){document.querySelectorAll('.question-option').forEach(n=>n.hidden=!n.dataset.question.includes(t.value.toLowerCase()))}if(t.id==='find-page')nav();if(t.id==='job-description')state.jobText=t.value});
document.addEventListener('change',e=>{const t=e.target;if(t.dataset.compare!==undefined){const i=Number(t.dataset.compare);state.compare=t.checked?[...new Set([...state.compare,i])]:state.compare.filter(n=>n!==i);$('#comparebar').hidden=!state.compare.length;$('#compare-count').textContent=state.compare.length+' roles selected';$('#comparebar button').disabled=state.compare.length<2}if(t.id==='resume-layout'){state.resumeLayout=t.value;render()}if(t.id==='admin-format'){state.adminFormat=t.value;render()}if(t.id==='history-role'){state.historyRole=t.value;render()}});
document.addEventListener('submit',e=>{if(e.target.id==='job-form'){e.preventDefault();state.jobText=$('#job-description').value;if(state.jobText.trim().length<80){$('#job-error').textContent='Include the responsibilities and requirements, not just the title.';return}state.jobResult=true;render()}if(e.target.id==='auth-form'){e.preventDefault();toast('Sign-in design only. No credentials were submitted.')}if(e.target.id==='cohort-form'){e.preventDefault();const f=new FormData(e.target);const draft=`Ascend access request\n\nOrganisation: ${f.get('org')}\nName: ${f.get('name')}\nEmail: ${f.get('email')}\nRole: ${f.get('role')}\nAudience: ${state.page==='college'?'College':'Employer'}`;modal(`<h2>Your email draft is ready.</h2><p>In the live flow, the next step opens your email app. Copying a draft is a fallback; it is not a submitted request.</p><label>Draft<textarea id="request-draft" rows="9" readonly>${esc(draft)}</textarea></label><div class="actions">${button('Copy draft','copy-request')}${button('Back to form','close-dialog','secondary')}</div><p class="note">No email is sent by this preview.</p>`)}});
$('#notes-toggle').onclick=()=>{state.notes=!state.notes;$('#review-notes').hidden=!state.notes;$('#notes-toggle').textContent=state.notes?'Hide review notes':'Show review notes';$('#notes-toggle').setAttribute('aria-expanded',String(state.notes))};
$('#device').onclick=()=>{state.mobile=!state.mobile;$('#deviceframe').classList.toggle('mobile',state.mobile);$('#device').textContent=state.mobile?'Desktop view':'Mobile view';$('#device').setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(state.mobile))};
$('#theme').onclick=()=>{setTheme(document.documentElement.dataset.theme==='dark'?'light':'dark');if(state.page==='settings')render()};
$('.dialog-close').onclick=()=>$('#detail-dialog').close();$('#detail-dialog').addEventListener('click',e=>{if(e.target===$('#detail-dialog')){const r=e.target.getBoundingClientRect();if(e.clientX<r.left||e.clientX>r.right||e.clientY<r.top||e.clientY>r.bottom)e.target.close()}});
window.addEventListener('hashchange',()=>{if($('#detail-dialog').open)$('#detail-dialog').close();go()});
try{setTheme(localStorage.getItem('ascend:review-theme')==='light'?'light':'dark')}catch{setTheme('dark')}
go();
